{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:buffalo-veda", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "At Paiṭhaṇ, when the brahmins scorned the outcast siblings and pointed to a passing buffalo saying a name means nothing, Jñāneśvar laid his hand on the buffalo and it recited the Veda — showing one Self in all.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "dispute", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:jnanesvar"], "disputes": ["dsp:caste-and-the-varkari-saints"], "concepts": ["cpt:bhakti-and-caste"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:cokha-bones", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "When Cokhāmeḷā died under a collapsing wall, Nāmdev knew his bones among the dead because they murmured 'Viṭṭhala', and buried them before the Paṇḍharpūr temple.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["death-dying", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:cokhamela", "tch:namdev"], "concepts": ["cpt:bhakti-and-caste"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:eknath-donkey", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "Carrying Gaṅgā water to Rāmeśvaram for the god, Eknāth poured it into the mouth of a dying donkey, saying the Lord of Rāmeśvaram had received it there.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:eknath"], "concepts": ["cpt:marks-of-the-saint"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:eknath-patience", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "A man spat on Eknāth each time he came up from his bath in the Godāvarī; Eknāth bathed again without anger, more than a hundred times, until the man fell at his feet.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:eknath"], "concepts": ["cpt:marks-of-the-saint"], "obstacles": ["obs:ari-sadvarga"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:flying-wall", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "Cāṅgadev came riding a tiger with a snake for a whip; the siblings, seated on a wall, made it move to meet him; seeing mastery over the inert surpass his power over beasts, he was humbled and became Muktābāī's disciple.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:cangadeva-vatesvar", "tch:muktabai", "tch:jnanesvar"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhis-inferior-to-devotion"], "obstacles": ["obs:siddhi-abhimana"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:gora-pots", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "At a gathering of saints Gorā tapped each head with his pot-testing stick and declared Nāmdev alone 'unbaked'; Viṭṭhala told Nāmdev he lacked a guru and sent him to Visobā Khecar, who, found resting his feet on a liṅga, bade Nāmdev put them where God was not — and a liṅga rose wherever he set them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:gora-kumbhar", "tch:namdev", "tch:visoba-khecar"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:namdev-feeds-vitthala", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "The child Nāmdev, sent to offer food at the temple, wept and threatened to die until Viṭṭhala ate from his hand.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:namdev"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:narahari-sonar", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "Narahari the goldsmith, devoted only to Śiva, blindfolded himself to measure Viṭṭhala's waist, felt the form of Śiva, and on unbinding his eyes saw Viṭṭhala; he understood Hari and Hara to be one.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:narahari-sonar"], "concepts": ["cpt:vitthala-of-pandharpur", "cpt:harihara-identity"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:bhaktavijaya:tukaram-notebooks", "source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "location": {"ref": "Bhaktavijaya (chapter not recalled)"}, "paraphrase": "Rāmeśvar Bhaṭṭ, holding that a śūdra may not expound the Veda's meaning, ordered Tukārām to sink his notebooks in the Indrāyaṇī; Tukārām sat fasting on the bank for thirteen days, the notebooks rose dry, and Rāmeśvar became his disciple.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "powers-experiences", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:tukaram", "tch:ramesvar-bhatt"], "disputes": ["dsp:caste-and-the-varkari-saints"], "concepts": ["cpt:bhakti-and-caste"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Tradition's account as told by Mahīpati.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
